From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8150-xiaomi-raphael: drop the IPA node

The IPA node (&ipa) only exists on the soc/qualcomm-sm8150 branch
"andrew/6.16-ipa", not on the main development branch the rest of this
tree tracks, so the board DTS cannot resolve the label as written.
Drop the override so the DTB builds. Consequence: no IPA -> no mobile data.

---
index eaf9f7f..a45d0d7 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-raphael.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-raphael.dts
@@ -549,13 +549,6 @@
 	};
 };
 
-&ipa {
-	status = "okay";
-	qcom,gsi-loader = "self";
-	memory-region = <&ipa_fw_mem>;
-	firmware-name = "qcom/sm8150/Xiaomi/raphael/ipa_fws.mbn";
-};
-
 &mdss_dsi0 {
 	vdda-supply = <&vdda_mipi_dsi0_1p2>;
 	status = "okay";
